        "mode": "dark"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "k01A4M",
      "x": 1460,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Note A",
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "content": "A — Плотная таблица. One line, about 32 pt at every width. Columns: date, title, duration, a 64 pt status cell (summary pending, failed, notes eye; the ⋯ button takes its place on hover). The title truncates with an ellipsis and never wraps. Narrow (< 600): duration column drops, date shortens to dd.MM. Actions: double-click or Return opens; context menu (shown) holds everything else; ⌘⌫ deletes. Header sorts by column. Closest to native Table / Finder list."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "YzMTV",
      "x": 1460,
      "y": 1000,
      "name": "Note B",
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "content": "B — Две строки (Mail). Fixed two-line row, about 48 pt: title + relative time on line 1, duration and summary state as text on line 2 (failed in red). Same layout at every width, so narrow costs nothing. Less dense: ~11 calls per 600 pt vs ~17 for A. Status reads as words, not icons."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "VQI1x",
      "x": 1460,
      "y": 2000,
      "name": "Note C",
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "content": "C — По дням (Notes). Day headers ‘Сегодня / Вчера / Пятница, 17 октября’ replace the date column; rows show only the time (40 pt), title, duration, status, about 28 pt. Most title width of the three. Narrow drops duration. Sorting is chronological only."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "zFSZf",
      "x": 1460,
      "y": 3000,
      "name": "Note shared",
      "width": 360,
      "height": 260,
      "content": "Shared in every direction: no reserved action column; actions live in the context menu, on keys (Return, Space for notes, ⌘R rename, ⌘⌫ delete) and in one ⋯ button that shows on hover inside the status cell. Retry summary moves from a link under the title to the context menu and the failed icon. The footer hint about renaming goes away. A row's height never depends on the title or status. Open: whether A's narrow layout should switch to B's two-line row instead of dropping columns."
    }
  ],
